[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=kwinshot (serpantinum)
Comment=Grants the screenshot helper KWin's restricted ScreenShot2 interface, for the overlay's freeze

# KWin hands out org.kde.KWin.ScreenShot2 per executable: it canonicalises the
# caller's /proc/<pid>/exe, looks for an installed desktop file whose Exec is that
# same binary, and reads X-KDE-DBUS-Restricted-Interfaces off it. So this is a file
# of its own — Exec has to be the helper, not /usr/bin/quickshell — and the path is
# absolute, written in by ../install.sh at install time.
#
# Per executable means per copy of the binary. A shell started as `qs -p <checkout>`
# runs the checkout's kwinshot, not the installed one, so install.sh writes this file
# twice when the two differ: org.serpantinum.kwinshot.desktop for the installed tree
# and org.serpantinum.kwinshot-dev.desktop for the checkout.
#
# It buys that binary the whole interface — the helper only calls CaptureArea,
# CaptureActiveScreen and CaptureWorkspace: pixels straight from the compositor
# instead of launching Spectacle for the overlay's freeze. Without it the helper is
# told NoAuthorized and the overlay falls back to Spectacle, slower but intact.
#
# Delete this file to revoke that, then run: kbuildsycoca6
Exec=@KWINSHOT@
NoDisplay=true
X-KDE-DBUS-Restricted-Interfaces=org.kde.KWin.ScreenShot2
